-- title:
--   Concatenating finite ordered groups
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let group sizes $c_p$ be given for parents $p<n$.
--
--   1. **Total and offsets.** $\mathrm{total}=\sum_pc_p$ and $\mathrm{offset}(p)=\sum_{q<p}c_q$.
--   2. **Encoding.** The local index $i$ in group $p$ goes to
--   $$
--   \mathrm{offset}(p)+i ,
--   $$
--   an order-respecting bijection from pairs $(p,i)$ onto $\{0..\mathrm{total}-1\}$.
--   3. **Parent map.** The group of a global index. It is monotone, and surjective when all groups are nonempty, and sums over a parent fiber are sums over the group.
--   4. **Retention.** Order embeddings inside each group assemble into one global order embedding that preserves parents.
